WEBVTT

00:06:59.943 --> 00:07:04.090
yeah, that would sort of show up
and get in the way sometimes.

00:07:04.114 --> 00:07:07.718
CA: I mean, you explain in the book
that shyness, per se,

00:07:07.742 --> 00:07:11.971
is not necessarily
the same as introversion.

00:07:11.995 --> 00:07:13.374
Explain that difference.

00:07:13.398 --> 00:07:17.321
SC: Yeah. I always think of the book
and the work that I do

00:07:17.345 --> 00:07:20.840
as being about both
shyness and introversion

00:07:20.864 --> 00:07:24.580
and the whole constellation of traits
that goes along with this way of being,

00:07:24.604 --> 00:07:26.401
even though they really are separate.

00:07:26.425 --> 00:07:28.556
And you could be
an introvert who's not shy,

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:32.705
and you could be a super extrovert
who is shy in new situations.